  :how "Build a static key-flow graph over the three scope paths. (1) For every map literal {:k v ...} passed as an argument, record its literal key set W and the callee. (2) For the callee (and everything it passes that map to under the same symbol), record the key set R of reads: :keys destructuring, (:k m), (get-in m [:k ...]), contains?, select-keys with literal vectors. (3) Report (a) keys written but never read anywhere transitively — the :strategic-selection-fn / :include-advisory-lanes? class, including docstring-only mentions; (b) keys read but never written on any path — the nil-deref class; (c) for known producer/consumer pairs declared in an allowlist (scan-data→render-war-machine, judgement→trace-record, active-mission→tick-mission-focus, opts→judge), a diff of W vs R so an added key with no reader clause in a cond-> copy-list (trace.clj) is flagged at review time. Docstring references to keyword names should be matched too: a key documented but never read is the strongest signal of retired-behavior drift. (4) REVIEW ADDITION (claude-4): when a write-only key is found, run git log -S on the READER to date its death — removal residue (reader died with the feature) needs a comment/test cleanup, while a never-honoured option needs a behaviour fix; one command separates them. (5) REVIEW ADDITION: flag TESTS whose assertions are about a call's ARGUMENTS (e.g. full_loop_runner_test.clj:2675 asserting (false? (:include-advisory-lanes? @seen))) with no assertion about the callee's EFFECT — an argument-asserting test is what lets a drifted key list survive a removal looking green; grep for assertions of the form 'the callee received X' without a corresponding effect assertion."
  :false-positive-risk "Deliberately-dead-by-protocol keys (present-only keys whose consumer is a later tick reading the persisted trace, e.g. :policy-precision-state's read-side guard) will look writer-only unless the checker also scans trace readers; optional opts (:trace? etc. read via destructure defaults) need the transitive-pass treatment; select-keys used for shape-normalization rather than mirroring (mission-value-weights, which self-checks its key set) should be allowlisted."}}
